<title>JAPAN: Stable forex moves desirable - Japan trade minister.</title>
<headline>Stable forex moves desirable - Japan trade minister.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stable foreign exchange movements are desirable for economic activities in Japan, Trade Minister Shinji Sato told a news conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Japan will keep careful watch on recent currency movements in which the yen has appreciated against the dollar, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Basically, stable currency moves are desirable for Japan's economic activities but it is too early to say if the recent rise of the yen will affect Japan's trading patterns,&quot; Sato said.</p>
</text>
